  "title": "V. Gordon Childe",
  "summary": "Vere Gordon Childe was an Australian-born archaeologist of European prehistory, born in Sydney in 1892 and dead in 1957. He held the Abercromby chair of prehistoric archaeology at Edinburgh and later directed the Institute of Archaeology in London. His books include The Dawn of European Civilization and Man Makes Himself, and he is associated with the ideas of the Neolithic and Urban Revolutions.",
